====1F (front)====
Enter [[Meteor Falls]] and scale the upper waterfall to reach the second part of 1F.

====1F (back)====
A series of ledges restrict movement from this direction, so go northeast and climb down the ladder.

====B1F (front)====
A short distance away, you find a fork in the road.
* Taking the northwest ladder leads to the previous chamber, where another ladder leads back here. This lets you {{m|Surf}} across the water to the north doorway, which leads to a tiny chamber with {{TM|02|Dragon Claw}}. It's also the only area where wild {{p|Bagon}} can be found. Surf southeast from that chamber to another doorway which leads to a part of the entrance chamber that holds a [[PP Up]].
* Taking the southwest ladder leads to the far northwest hill in the entrance chamber. Collect {{TM|23|Iron Tail}}.

==Ever Grande City (south)==
[[File:Ever Grande City E.png|thumb|left|Ever Grande City]]

High above the ocean, [[Ever Grande City]] is lush with grass and flowers. The large waterfall makes it impossible to reach the city itself without a Pokémon able to {{m|Waterfall|scale}} the cascading waters. The island is divided by {{ho|Victory Road}}, which runs through a large mountain at the center of the isle. Visit the Pokémon Center to make your preparations before braving this final challenge on the road to the [[Pokémon League]], also in here inside is [[Scott]] to talk with him in his last localization before completing the game.

