===1F===
Head north under the first two bridges and climb the north-northwest stairway. Turn east and cross over these next two bridges to reach a [[Max Elixir]] on a ledge to the east. Jump the ledge and head to the northwest, battling Cooltrainer Albert on the way. Climb the west-central stairway and cross the bridge, and [[Wally]] appears from the south. His defeat in your previous battle forced him to become stronger, and you find that the sickly, weak-willed kid you met back in [[Petalburg City]] is no more. In his place stands a confident Trainer, ready to show off how much training he's done!

====VS Wally====
Wally leads with his {{p|Altaria}}, a {{2t|Dragon|Flying}} type that is especially vulnerable to {{t|Ice}} attacks. It can raise its {{stat|Attack}} and {{stat|Speed}} with {{m|Dragon Dance}}, so use super-effective moves to take it down before it becomes a major threat. {{p|Delcatty}} may be his weakest Pokémon, but it can still cause problems with {{m|Sing}}, {{m|Charm}}, and its {{a|Cute Charm}} Ability. Its stats aren't very threatening, but knock it out quickly to avoid these pitfalls. With moves like {{m|Toxic}} and {{m|Leech Seed}}, his {{p|Roselia}} can tip the battle in his favor as time goes on. Knock it out with {{t|Fire}}, {{t|Ice}}, {{t|Flying}}, or {{t|Psychic}} moves. {{p|Magneton}} can be a major threat due to its high {{stat|Special Attack}}; strike it with {{t|Ground}} moves to take it down. Finally, Wally resorts to using his {{p|Gardevoir}}. {{m|Psychic}} and {{m|Future Sight}} are strong attacks that receive a [[same-type attack bonus]], and {{m|Calm Mind}} can boost its damage output to dangerous levels. Use {{t|Dark}}, {{t|Ghost}}, and {{t|Bug}} moves to knock it out and win the battle.

